The '''Castejón Metro Maraña Line''' ({{Lang-bl|Linia de Metro de Castejón a Maranya}}) is a [[W:Rapid transit|subway]] line in [[Castejón]], Balisca, operated by [[Castejón Metro]]. The line runs between [[Prosperidad Station]] in [[Charxes]] and [[Golondrinas Station]] in [[Trinacria]], with a branch line between [[El Cañaveral Station]] and [[Aeropuerto T2 Station]] ([[Concordia International Airport|Concordia Airport]]). The official name is '''Line 3 Maraña Line'''.

The line was named after the [[Maraña]] barrio in the [[Coruxón]] borough, under which it passes. On maps, diagrams and signboards, the line is shown using the color red, and its stations are given numbers using the letters "M" for the main line and "Mb" for the branch line. 

